# Findash — allow the `deploy` user to install findash.service from CD.
#
# Install to /etc/sudoers.d/findash-unit-install, mode 0440, owned root:root.
# Validate with `visudo -c -f` BEFORE moving it into place — a syntax error in
# this directory locks sudo for everyone on the box.
#
# Issue: ingamartinez/personal-financial-dashboard#799
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BE PLAIN ABOUT WHAT THIS GRANT IS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It is root-equivalent for `deploy`. `deploy` controls the contents of the
# unit installed below and already holds `systemctl restart findash.service`
# (see findash-deploy in this same directory), so it can run an arbitrary
# ExecStart= as root. The literal paths bound WHICH file gets written, not
# what can be put inside it.
#
# This is NOT a new power. /etc/sudoers.d/findash-deploy already grants
# `deploy ALL=(findash) NOPASSWD: ALL`, and findash-redis-provision already
# grants the same install-a-unit-as-root pattern for redis.service. The real
# enforcement boundary is PR review of infra/systemd/findash.service, branch
# protection on `main`, custody of the DEPLOY_SSH_KEY secret, and who may
# dispatch the Deploy workflow — not sudoers narrowness.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL (#799)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Before #799 nothing re-installed findash.service after infra/bootstrap.sh
# laid it down on a fresh droplet. CD only ran `systemctl restart`. The repo
# copy and the live file drifted silently for months — the live unit was still
# the 2026-04-18 bootstrap copy, missing the TimeoutStopSec=10 change that
# merged with #185.
#
# That made the #796 memory caps (MemoryHigh=640M / MemoryMax=768M) a
# hand-placed artifact rather than something reproducible from this repo:
# reprovisioning the droplet, re-running bootstrap.sh, or assuming a deploy
# syncs the unit would all have produced a machine without them.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THE STAGING PATHS ARE UNDER /home/deploy AND NOT /tmp
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same reason as findash-redis-provision — see that file for the full
# write-up. Short version: /tmp is drwxrwxrwt and this droplet has other local
# principals with a real /tmp view outside any PrivateTmp sandbox (the
# /etc/cron.d backup jobs run as findash, photoshowcase and zyeth; cron does
# not apply PrivateTmp=). Any of them could pre-create the staged path and
# rewrite it before the privileged install, getting root to install their
# content. /home/deploy is 0750 with an empty `deploy` group and
# /home/deploy/staging is 0700, so only `deploy` and root can traverse it.
#
# `install -m 0644 -o root -g root` rather than `mv`: mode and ownership are
# stated explicitly instead of inherited from the staged inode.
#
# No sudo grant for reading or comparing the live unit — it is 0644 root:root,
# so the pipeline's drift gate uses a plain unprivileged `cmp -s`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two source paths, both literal, no wildcards:
#
#   findash.service       — the repo copy, scp'd by the "Install findash unit"
#                           step in .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#   findash.service.prev  — a snapshot of the live unit taken by the "Capture
#                           rollback state" step BEFORE any mutation, so
#                           "Rollback on failure" can restore it byte-for-byte.
#
# The .prev grant is what makes the unit-install window rollback-safe. Without
# it a failed deploy could leave a new unit paired with an old release.
#
# /usr/bin/systemctl is the same binary the sibling findash-deploy file
# references as /bin/systemctl (/bin -> /usr/bin, Ubuntu 24.04 usrmerge).
deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/install -m 0644 -o root -g root /home/deploy/staging/findash.service /etc/systemd/system/findash.service
deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/install -m 0644 -o root -g root /home/deploy/staging/findash.service.prev /etc/systemd/system/findash.service
deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl daemon-reload
